        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\"></td><td colspan=\"3\">Relevant credentials</td></tr><tr><td>Security appliances</td><td>Comment</td><td>EVCC (EV)</td><td>SECC (EVSE) private SECC (for PE only)</td><td>Secondary actor</td></tr><tr><td>DC/AC charging with PnC\n- DC/AC charging with transport security\n- contracts based payment, with meter status receipt\n- individual / dynamic tariff tables for customer contract certificate installation via EVSE is not supported contract certificate validation by SECC</td><td>- TLS authentication of SECC\n- TLS authentication of EVCC\n- contract authentication on application layer\n- TLS based confidential data exchange between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering)\n- TLS based integrity of data between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering)\n- meter receipt signing based on contract key pair\nAppl.Layer: AES for data encryption, ECDH used for key exchange, ECC for digital signature for tariff signing\nTLS: AES used for stream/session encryption, ECDH used for key exchange</td><td>Vehicle leaf key pair (vehicle leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by an OEM root CA or a V2G root CA\nall vehicle sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the vehicle certificate\nV2G root CA certificate(s)\ncontract key pair (contract private key and certificate for contract based payment) certified by a CA which can be certified by a V2G root CA.\nAll eMSP sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the contract certificate</td><td>SECC leaf key pair (up to 10 generations depending on the aging V2G RootKey) (SECC leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by a V2G root CA\nall CSO sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the SECC certificate\nOCSP response ticket(s) from the corresponding CSO-sub-CA and V2G root CA\nOEM root CA certificate(s) (if not below a V2G root.\nV2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise)\nall eMSP root CA certificates of the eMSPs the CSO has contract agreements with.</td><td>eMSP root CA certificate (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise)\nall eMSP-sub-CA certificate of the certificate chain below the eMSP-sub-CA key\npair issuing contract certificates\neMSP sub-CA key pair (SA private key and certificate) for contract certificate signing</td></tr></table>",
